{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "613504-1b7e-4a9c-9f21-library-jwt",
    "name": "Librería en línea · JWT (UDEM SC-2236 · 613504)",
    "description": "Demostración del control de acceso por JWT en los microservicios de la librería.\n\nREGLA QUE SE DEMUESTRA (la \"trampa\"): la autorización NO se decide por ruta, se decide por MÉTODO HTTP.\n  · GET /books y GET /books/{isbn}  -> PÚBLICOS (cualquiera consulta el catálogo)\n  · POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE     -> PROTEGIDOS (exigen Authorization: Bearer <JWT> del servicio login)\n\nCarpetas:\n  00  La trampa: la misma ruta, dos autorizaciones distintas\n  01  Obtener el JWT (captcha -> registro -> login)\n  02  Catálogo público (sin token)\n  03  Escrituras protegidas (con Bearer)\n  04  Sesión, introspección y refresh token\n  05  Ataques contra el JWT (deben fallar)\n  06  Salud e instancia\n\nAntes de correr: selecciona el entorno \"Librería JWT · local (613504)\" y ejecuta las carpetas en orden (00, 01, 02, ...). Las variables access_token / refresh_token / captcha_id se van llenando solas con los scripts de test.\n\nEl secreto HS256 vive en el ENTORNO ({{jwt_secret}}), no en la colección: igual que en producción, donde la clave va en variables de entorno o en un secret manager y nunca en el código fuente.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url_login", "value": "http://172.32.132.174:5000" },
    { "key": "base_url_books", "value": "http://172.32.132.174:5001" },
    { "key": "isbn", "value": "" },
    { "key": "isbn_alias", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 · La trampa: la misma ruta, dos autorizaciones distintas",
      "description": "La misma URL /books responde distinto según el MÉTODO HTTP. Esto es exactamente lo que se pide: proteger las escrituras sin cerrar el catálogo.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /books  (público, sin token) -> 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('GET /books responde 200 SIN token (catálogo público)', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('La respuesta anuncia los métodos públicos', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Public-Methods')).to.eql('GET, HEAD, OPTIONS');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('El catálogo trae libros', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().books.length).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url_books}}/books?format=json", "host": ["{{base_url_books}}"], "path": ["books"], "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "json" }] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /books  (protegido, SIN token) -> 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('POST /books SIN token responde 401 Unauthorized', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Trae el encabezado WWW-Authenticate: Bearer', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate')).to.include('Bearer');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('El código de error es TOKEN_REQUIRED', function () {",
                  "  var b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  var codigo = (b.error && b.error.code) || b.code;",
                  "  pm.expect(codigo).to.eql('TOKEN_REQUIRED');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"isbn\": \"SIN-TOKEN-613504\",\n  \"title\": \"Este alta debe fallar sin token\",\n  \"price\": 100,\n  \"stock\": 1,\n  \"publication_year\": 2026,\n  \"format_id\": 7,\n  \"category_id\": 8,\n  \"author_ids\": [2],\n  \"genre_ids\": []\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url_books}}/books", "host": ["{{base_url_books}}"], "path": ["books"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /api/book/insert  (ALIAS, SIN token) -> 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('El alias de escritura tampoco es una puerta trasera: 401', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"isbn\": \"ALIAS-SIN-TOKEN-613504\",\n  \"title\": \"Alias sin token\",\n  \"price\": 100,\n  \"stock\": 1,\n  \"publication_year\": 2026,\n  \"format_id\": 7,\n  \"category_id\": 8,\n  \"author_ids\": [2],\n  \"genre_ids\": []\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url_books}}/api/book/insert", "host": ["{{base_url_books}}"], "path": ["api", "book", "insert"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "01 · Obtener el JWT (captcha -> registro -> login)",
      "description": "Aquí nace el token. El login valida las credenciales contra PostgreSQL y devuelve un access_token (JWT, 15 min) y un refresh_token (opaco, 7 días).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /captcha  (público)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Resuelve el CAPTCHA aritmético (llega como '¿Cuánto es 4 - 1?').",
                  "var j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.environment.set('captcha_id', j.data.captcha_id);",
                  "var m = /(\\d+)\\s*([+\\-*])\\s*(\\d+)/.exec(j.data.question);",
                  "var a = parseInt(m[1], 10), b = parseInt(m[3], 10), op = m[2];",
                  "var r = op === '+' ? a + b : (op === '-' ? a - b : a * b);",
                  "pm.environment.set('captcha_answer', String(r));",
                  "pm.environment.set('captcha_question', j.data.question);",
                  "pm.test('El servicio entrega un desafío CAPTCHA', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.environment.get('captcha_id')).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('Desafío: ' + pm.environment.get('captcha_question') +",
                  "            ' -> respuesta ' + pm.environment.get('captcha_answer'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url_login}}/captcha?format=json", "host": ["{{base_url_login}}"], "path": ["captcha"], "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "json" }] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /register  (alta del usuario de prueba)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// 201 la primera vez; 409 si el usuario demo ya existía de una corrida anterior.",
                  "pm.test('Registro 201 Created (o 409 si el usuario demo ya existía)', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"nombre\": \"Postman\",\n  \"apellido_paterno\": \"JWT\",\n  \"apellido_materno\": \"Demo\",\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"captcha_id\": \"{{captcha_id}}\",\n  \"captcha_answer\": \"{{captcha_answer}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url_login}}/register?format=json", "host": ["{{base_url_login}}"], "path": ["register"], "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "json" }] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /captcha  (nuevo desafío para el login)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
              "type": "text/javascript",
              "exec": [
                "// Desafío nuevo para el login.",
                "var j = pm.response.json();",
                "pm.environment.set('captcha_id', j.data.captcha_id);",
                "var m = /(\\d+)\\s*([+\\-*])\\s*(\\d+)/.exec(j.data.question);",
                "var a = parseInt(m[1], 10), b = parseInt(m[3], 10), op = m[2];",
                "var r = op === '+' ? a + b : (op === '-' ? a - b : a * b);",
                "pm.environment.set('captcha_answer', String(r));",
                "pm.environment.set('captcha_question', j.data.question);",
                "console.log('Nuevo desafío: ' + j.data.question + ' -> ' + r);"
              ]
            }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url_login}}/captcha?format=json", "host": ["{{base_url_login}}"], "path": ["captcha"], "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "json" }] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /login  -> aquí nace el JWT",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "var cuerpo = pm.response.json();",
                  "var sesion = cuerpo.data.session;",
                  "pm.environment.set('access_token', sesion.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('refresh_token', sesion.refresh_token);",
                  "pm.test('Login 200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve un access_token con formato JWT (3 segmentos)', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(sesion.access_token.split('.').length).to.eql(3);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('El esquema es Bearer y el algoritmo HS256', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(sesion.token_type).to.eql('Bearer');",
                  "  pm.expect(sesion.algorithm).to.eql('HS256');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('El access token dura 15 minutos y el refresh 7 días', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(sesion.expires_in).to.eql(900);",
                  "  pm.expect(sesion.refresh_expires_in).to.eql(604800);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('El refresh_token es distinto del access_token', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(sesion.refresh_token).to.not.eql(sesion.access_token);",
                  "});",
                  "// Inspección del payload (el payload va CODIFICADO, no cifrado).",
                  "var payload = JSON.parse(CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.stringify(",
                  "  CryptoJS.enc.Base64.parse(sesion.access_token.split('.')[1]",
                  "    .replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/'))));",
                  "console.log('JWT claims: ' + JSON.stringify(payload));",
                  "pm.test('Los claims del RFC 7519 están presentes', function () {",
                  "  ['iss', 'aud', 'sub', 'exp', 'iat', 'nbf'].forEach(function (c) {",
                  "    pm.expect(payload, 'claim ' + c).to.have.property(c);",
                  "  });",
                  "  pm.expect(payload.iss).to.eql('library-login');",
                  "  pm.expect(payload.aud).to.eql('library-api');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"captcha_id\": \"{{captcha_id}}\",\n  \"captcha_answer\": \"{{captcha_answer}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url_login}}/login?format=json", "host": ["{{base_url_login}}"], "path": ["login"], "query": [{ "key": "format", "value": "json" }] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
